title: Chat requests have no timeout on the Net::Async::HTTP backend (user_agent_timeout
  only reaches LWP)
updated: 2026-09-25T18:20:21Z
---

From k276: Role::HTTP user_agent_timeout configures the LWP user agent only; on the Net::Async::HTTP backend a chat request has no timeout, so a hanging provider stalls the Future forever (knarr/skeid/raider hang). Apply user_agent_timeout (when set) to the async backend too (Net::Async::HTTP timeout/stall_timeout, or a loop timeout_future race like k276), consider a sane default for async. Streaming: stall timeout (no bytes for N s) rather than total. Tests with a local daemon that never answers / stalls mid-stream.
